},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:16:47-07:00","id":887544,"title":"","content":"I suppose you might look at the Kickstarters for similar projects and see what people asked for or really made people get interested. I know art is a big deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-10-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T18:07:20-07:00","id":888718,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> Thanks for the advice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T18:30:32-07:00","id":890320,"title":"","content":"Retracted Statement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11693,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:56:43-07:00","id":890822,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be perfectly honest; your weird insistence on intense secrecy doesn't make for a super compelling thread, and you're not gonna get a lot from people here if we aren't allowed to know what your game is. All you've basically said so far is &quot;it's kinda like the World of Darkness but different,&quot; and that just doesn't give us enoug to give meaningful feedback or compelling ideas. <br /> <br /> Why not give us your 'elevator pitch,' the one or two sentence idea for what this project is that's simple enough for a perfect stranger to understand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T19:49:52-07:00","id":890932,"title":"","content":"Retracted Statement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11693,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:01:18-07:00","id":891354,"title":"","content":"So far you're still just finding different ways to say &quot;it's like WoD, but different.&quot; Without knowing more specific details, the only advice I think anyone can give is &quot;make it less like WoD&quot; because the people who want WoD already have it, so the more you can make it stand on its own apart from WoD, the more successful it will be. Without more specific details about your project it's impossible to give more specific feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T14:17:46-07:00","id":894310,"title":"","content":"What does &quot;project&quot; mean? Are you writing a setting to play games in? A setting for fiction? Is this something you want to sell?<br /> <br /> With a role-playing game, generally speaking I'd advise you to steal ideas you like aggressively. If you think it'd be more fun to play in your setting if you include an idea from the World of Darkness wholecloth, go for it and see what your players think. You needn't worry about originality unless you're trying to appeal to a publisher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T19:24:56-07:00","id":894500,"title":"","content":"Retracted Statement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11693,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T23:05:19-07:00","id":894571,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, but this whole topic is completely baffling to me. Imagine if someone posted a thread on some D&amp;D forums &quot;Hey, I'm working on this project where I want to have all the different high fantasy races like elves and dwarves and stuff. The elves are the most developed part right now, and they're kind of inspired by D&amp;D as well as Tolkien and especially folklore, both in what I do and don't want them to do. I really don't know what I want to do with this project, but I can't tell you anything more about it. I would really appreciate any advice anyone has on how to make it good.&quot; You would have no idea where to even begin because the whole thing is so nebulous and vague, beyond the implication that it's kinda like D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T05:39:15-07:00","id":896027,"title":"","content":"Retracted Statement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11693,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 02-13-2019, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T06:01:50-07:00","id":896038,"title":"","content":"It doesn't break any rules, it's just very strange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T20:11:16-07:00","id":900617,"title":"","content":"Fortunately for you, if you don't know what you're going to do with this project of yours, it's not really possible for it to be good or bad, unless it's offensive somehow. You can pretty much do anything you want with it until you decide on a medium. When you know if you want it to be a film or a RPG or whatever, then we can tell you what's good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T02:02:33-07:00","id":914720,"title":"","content":"If it helps, here are some of the other authors and groups working in this vein:<br /> <br /> * In his <b>Felix Gomez</b> series, Mario Acevedo is exploring what would happen if the oWoD Camarilla discovered there were aliens on Earth, doing . . . something. The main character is a veteran who got Embraced during the Iraq War, and now works as a private eye. Roughly half the books focus on the aliens and vampires slowly becoming aware of each other (tensions rising all the while), while the rest focus on Felix's other cases.<br /> <br /> * Mur Lafferty, a former White Wolf author, is working on tour guides for supernaturals. Or rather books about writing travel guides for the supernatural community, and the hijinks that ensue when they start asking questions. Starting with <b>The Shambling Guide to New York City</b>, her protagonist (a blackballed travel writer) gets recruited by a vampire (much to her surprise) to create the first travel guide to the hidden supernatural community in NYC. Strong nWoD/CoD influences, with some great excerpts from the travel book (I really, really want to open a bank account with the ravens).<br /> <br /> * Seanan McGuire's <b>October Daye</b> series reads almost exactly like a <i>Changeling: the Dreaming</i> series. Sure, there are some house rules thrown in . . . but it would not surprise me at all to learn that the protagonist used to be her PC in a <i>Changeling</i> campaign. Her <b>InCryptid</b> series is also pretty good, showcasing what would happen if a group of hunters suddenly went all Greeenpeace on behalf of the supernatural community. <br /> <br /> * Kelley Armstrong also works in a World of Darkness-ish vein. Her <b>Otherworld</b> series has a wild mix of supernaturals hiding in the shadows, where the multi-splat Council roughly counterbalances the sinister Cabals (dark mages who ruthlessly exploit other supernaturals). The first book, <i>Bitten</i>, was recently adapted as a SyFy series.<br /> <br /> * Carrie Vaughn, author of the <b>Kitty Norville</b> series, has an interesting series about a werewolf DJ who accidentally brings an end to the secrecy of the supernatural world - and kickstarts a war with an ancient Roman vampire. Chloe Neil (<i>Chicagoland Vampires</i>) and Charlaine Harris (<i>Sookie Stackhouse</i>/<i>True Blood</i>) explore similar ideas, albeit from the vampiric side of things<br /> <br /> * L.J. Smith's <b>Night World</b> books are a young adult series with a strong World of Darkness vibe. The end of the world is coming, and everyone is scrambling to find/control/kill the four Wild Powers who will determine whether the world is saved . . . or destroyed.<br /> <br /> A couple of others worth mentioning, albeit in a different framework: <br /> <br /> * Cubicle Seven is working on a series of variant <i>Call of Cthulhu</i> settings, where the PCs are spies recruited by the mysterious &quot;N&quot; to oppose the Mythos . . . as well as the enemies of the Allies/NATO/etc. The first, <i>Achtung! Cthulhu</i>, occurs during World War 2, while <i>World War Cthulhu</i> occurs during the Seventies (a.k.a. the height of the Cold War)<br /> <br /> * Tanya Huff has two overlapping series: <b>Keeper Chronicles</b> and <b>Enchantment Emporium</b>. Oddly, the two series have <i>exactly</i> the same plot outlines, but the books in the <i>Keeper Chronicles</i> are more . . . fun, while <i>Enchantment Emporium</i> skews far darker and more adult (as in &quot;cannibal witches who fuel their powers through bisexual orgies&quot; dark).<br /> <br /> * And Kim Harrison's <b>Rachel Morgan</b> (<i>Hollows</i>) series is basically World of Darkness meets <i>Shadowrun</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}